00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.100
Hey Andy, so how'd it go this time?

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.400
&gt;&gt; Pretty terribly.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.890
It probably took about ten times longer to get five cats working than it

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:08.770
did for two.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.250
Which doesn't make a lot of sense.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.220
&gt;&gt; Oh that's rough.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.645
&gt;&gt; Yeah. I had a lot of divs, if that's, is that a good thing?

00:00:14.645 --> 00:00:16.820
[LAUGH] A lot of divs with cats and

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.500
buttons and, you know, cat one, cat two, cat three.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.960
And I tried to, in the JavaScript file, iterate over all of those.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.370
And bind the buttons to the counters for

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.830
the different cats, but everything kept, kept getting down to the very last cat.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.830
&gt;&gt; Mm. That was that closure issue we were talking about.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:32.859
&gt;&gt; It was.

00:00:32.859 --> 00:00:36.760
That was where the 10x time increase came from, was figuring that out.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.637
But I mean it's working.

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:39.768
So, that's good.

00:00:39.768 --> 00:00:44.010
But, I, I, I don't want to keep making things this way.

